  "query_preview": "(Friday through Monday)...\nThe cooling trend will continue into the weekend with high\ntemperatures on Sunday 10 to 15 degrees below average for inland\nareas and 15 to 20 degrees below average for the mountains above\n6000 feet. High temperatures on Sunday for the coast and valleys\nwill be mostly in the 60s, for the mountains in the mid 30s to mid\n50s, and for the lower deserts in the lower to mid 70s.\n\nRainfall chances during the weekend are greatest for Saturday\nnight into Sunday morning and especially for late Saturday night \ninto Sunday morning. There remains a wide range in potential \nrainfall. ECMWF ensemble uncalibrated rainfall for San Diego has \n40 percent of members with 0.50 inch or less with 15 percent of \nensemble members having 2 inches or more. Half of ECMWF ensemble \nmembers have precipitable water at San Diego for late Saturday \nafternoon and Saturday evening increasing to 1.5 inch or greater, \nsomewhere around 250 percent of normal. \n\nFor Saturday morning through Sunday night, the chance for 1 inch \nor more of rainfall from the coast to the mountains ranges from 25\nto 30 percent for Orange and southwestern San Bernardino Counties\nto 35 to 40 percent for San Diego County.",
